        <definition>typedef rbusError_t(*) rbusTableAddRowHandler_t(rbusHandle_t handle, char const  *tableName, char const  *aliasName, uint32_t *instNum)</definition>
        <argsstring>(rbusHandle_t handle, char const *tableName, char const *aliasName, uint32_t *instNum)</argsstring>
        <name>rbusTableAddRowHandler_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>A table row add callback handler. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A provider must implement this handler to allow rows to be added to a table. The tableName parameter will end in &quot;.&quot; such as &quot;Device.IP.Interface.&quot; The aliasName parameter can optionally be used to specify a unique name for the row. A new row should be assigned a unique instance number and this number should be returned in the instNum output parameter. <linebreak/>
 <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>handle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bus Handle </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tableName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of a table (e.g. &quot;Device.IP.Interface.&quot;) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aliasName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>An optional name for the new row. Must be unique in the table. Can be NULL. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>instNum</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Output parameter where the instance number for the new row is returned </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>RBus error code as defined by <ref refid="group___common_1ga8fc1f9c96c061b20db5e56188296c8ef" kindref="member">rbusError_t</ref>. Possible values are: RBUS_ERROR_INVALID_INPUT </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/rbus.h" line="437" column="9" bodyfile="include/rbus.h" bodystart="437" bodyend="-1"/>
