      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group___providers_1gace673660999b800a3f21a239b5a40f8d" prot="public" static="no">
        <type><ref refid="group___common_1ga8fc1f9c96c061b20db5e56188296c8ef" kindref="member">rbusError_t</ref>(*)</type>
        <definition>typedef rbusError_t(*) rbusMethodHandler_t(rbusHandle_t handle, char const  *methodName, rbusObject_t inParams, rbusObject_t outParams, rbusMethodAsyncHandle_t asyncHandle)</definition>
        <argsstring>(rbusHandle_t handle, char const *methodName, rbusObject_t inParams, rbusObject_t outParams, rbusMethodAsyncHandle_t asyncHandle)</argsstring>
        <name>rbusMethodHandler_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>A method invocation callback handler. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A provider must implement this handler to support methods. <linebreak/>
 There are two ways to return a response to the method. The first is to set outParams in the handler and return RBUS_ERROR_SUCCESS. The second is to send the response later by storing the asyncHandle, returning RBUS_ERROR_ASYNC_RESPONSE from the handler, and later calling rbusMethod_SendAsyncResponse, passing the asyncHandle and output params. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>handle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bus Handle </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>methodName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the method being invoked ( e.g. &quot;Device.Foo.SomeFunc()&quot;); </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>inParams</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The input parameters to the functions </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>outParams</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The output/return parameters of the functions </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>asyncHandle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Handle passed to rbusMethod_SendAsyncResponse </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>RBus error code as defined by <ref refid="group___common_1ga8fc1f9c96c061b20db5e56188296c8ef" kindref="member">rbusError_t</ref>. Possible values are: RBUS_ERROR_INVALID_INPUT </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/rbus.h" line="482" column="9" bodyfile="include/rbus.h" bodystart="482" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="group___providers_1ga845118048502243dac351969766ce2e9" prot="public" static="no">
        <type><ref refid="group___common_1ga8fc1f9c96c061b20db5e56188296c8ef" kindref="member">rbusError_t</ref>(*)</type>
        <definition>typedef rbusError_t(*) rbusEventSubHandler_t(rbusHandle_t handle, rbusEventSubAction_t action, char const  *eventName, rbusFilter_t filter, int32_t interval, bool *autoPublish)</definition>
        <argsstring>(rbusHandle_t handle, rbusEventSubAction_t action, char const *eventName, rbusFilter_t filter, int32_t interval, bool *autoPublish)</argsstring>
        <name>rbusEventSubHandler_t</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>An event subcribe callback handler. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A provider will receive this callback when the first client subscribes to an event/filter pair or the last client unsubscribes to an event/filter pair or all subscribers have timed out due to max duration. Distribution of the event to multiple subscribers will be transparently handled by the library. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>handle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the rbus handle the event is registered to. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>action</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>whether the event is being subscribed or unsubscribe to. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>eventName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the fully qualified event name. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>filter</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>an the filter the subscriber would like the provider to use to decide when the event can be sent. This can be NULL if no filter was specified by the client. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>interval</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if non-zero, indicates that the event should be publish repeatedly every &apos;interval&apos; seconds. if a filter is also provided, it would publish only when the filter is triggered </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>autoPublish</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>output parameter used to disable the default behaviour where rbus automatically publishing events for provider data elements. When providers set autoPublish to true the value will be checked once per second and the maximum event rate is one event per two seconds. If faster eventing or real-time eventing is required providers can set autoPublish to false and implement a custom approach. For fastest response time and to avoid missing changes that occur faster than once per second, the preferred way is to use a callback triggered from the lowest level of code to detect a value change. This callback may be invoked by vendor code via a HAL API or other method. This callback can be received by the component that provides this event and used to send the publish message in real time. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>RBus error code as defined by <ref refid="group___common_1ga8fc1f9c96c061b20db5e56188296c8ef" kindref="member">rbusError_t</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/rbus.h" line="529" column="9" bodyfile="include/rbus.h" bodystart="529" bodyend="-1"/>
